{"seq":14,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-haiku-none-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:26:42.979Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"e07a6b6e7a60fd066a4f5c85018d2f5b2ba6e61ac4a2da997ca412e4e44b7d72","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"@Bettina Kroll, here's what I found. I read #coastal-team and #coastal-random, plus Moss's public Coastal digests. The Pellow Home Living tickets are left out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)**\n- Ticket #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length (Moss's Coastal cheat sheet).\n- Open item: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change (cheat sheet; no ticket number given).\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)**\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges (cheat sheet).\n- Request: patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift (11/2 pipeline digest; no ticket number given). Engineering has since provided a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher (cheat sheet).\n- Tide-table import macro failure on Terminal B (cheat sheet; the manual CSV patch above is the workaround).\n\n**Needs checking before Kwame's review:** the 11/2 digest links ticket #4419 to \"Kwame's port account\" for a barge slip 7 schedule sync, but the cheat sheet links #4419 to the Pellucid yard-dwell report. Both can't be right. Kwame or support should confirm which account #4419 belongs to.\n\nI found nothing on either account in the channels themselves."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
